# .Curatefile — Declarative Use-Case Dataset Curation & Teacher Distillation
# Launch interactively with: trainaya curate
# Or run non-interactively with: trainaya curate --non-interactive

# 1. Free-text description of your target Use-Case and decision policy
USE_CASE "Triage incoming customer support tickets and technical requests into actionable routing categories (refund, technical_help, billing_question, security_incident, general)"

# 2. Teacher Agent(s) to distill ('agy', 'claude', 'codex', 'gemini', 'ollama:<model>', 'ollaya:<model>')
#    Use comma-separated teachers (e.g. 'agy, claude') for multi-teacher consensus voting.
TEACHER agy

# 3. Workflow Mode:
#    - 'synth'    : Synthesize a tailored dataset & schema directly from USE_CASE
#    - 'reformat' : Reformat & distill an existing dataset (INPUT) for this USE_CASE
#    - 'augment'  : Reformat dataset + synthesize counterfactual hard-negative twins
MODE synth

# 4. Target Format & Decision Primitive ('choice', 'noul', 'score')
FORMAT decision
KIND choice

# Optional: Input dataset to reformat when MODE is 'reformat' or 'augment' (.jsonl, .csv, .json, .txt)
# INPUT ./data/raw_tickets.csv

# Optional: Explicit schema JSON file (if omitted, Teacher synthesizes it automatically from USE_CASE)
# SCHEMA ./data/schema.json

# 5. Output training dataset (ready for `trainaya adapt --data` or `trainaya train --data`)
OUTPUT ./data/curated_train.jsonl
COUNT 50

PARAMETER batch_size 10
PARAMETER min_confidence 0.85
PARAMETER add_hard_negatives true
